# THE IMPORTANT ONE.
#
# The counselling form is the site's only lead capture. Its success path builds
# the confirmation with ico('check') — but block5 is its own IIFE and never
# declares `ico`. Every other block declares its own copy; this one was missed.
#
# So the POST succeeded, the enquiry reached the office, and then the success
# handler threw a ReferenceError on the very next statement, landing in the
# catch that says "That did not send. Please call or email us." Every single
# visitor who filled the form correctly was told it had failed.
#
# Verified before and after in a real browser: the request returns 200 and is
# written to the enquiry log in both cases — only what the visitor is told
# changes.
patch(
    "index.html",
    "counselling form — declare ico() so the success message can render",
    'const $ = s => document.querySelector(s);\nconst ENDPOINT = "/send.php";\nconst TO = "info@glovels.com";',
    'const $ = s => document.querySelector(s);\n'
    "const ico = n => '<svg class=\"ico\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-'+n+'\"/></svg>';\n"
    'const ENDPOINT = "/send.php";\nconst TO = "info@glovels.com";\nconst PHONE = "+917093314089";',
)

# The failure message offered "Please call <a href="tel:"></a>or email us" — the
# number was derived by stripping non-digits out of an email address, so it was
# always empty, and the sentence read as broken markup at the worst moment.
patch(
    "index.html",
    "counselling form — the failure message carries a real phone number",
    "'<b>That did not send.</b> Please call <a href=\"tel:' + TO.replace(/[^0-9+]/g,'') + '\">'\n"
    "      + '</a>or email us, and your details are below so nothing is lost.'",
    "'<b>That did not send.</b> Please call <a href=\"tel:' + PHONE + '\">'\n"
    "      + '+91 70933 14089</a> or email us, and your details are below so nothing is lost.'",
    # A later patch rewrites this same line to read the number from the office's
    # own settings, so `new` stops being present verbatim once both have run.
    # The marker is the half that neither of them touches.
    marker="or email us, and your details are below so nothing is lost.",
)

